  "question": {
    "text": "The current through a coil of self inductance $\\mathrm{L}=2 m \\mathrm{H}$ is given by $\\mathrm{I}=t^2 e^{-t}$ at time $t$. How long it will take to make the e $\\mathrm{m} . f$ zero?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mckTe",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{~s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KBuht",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WuEQQ",
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{~s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uPCpg",
      "text": "$4 \\mathrm{~s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $\\mathrm{I}=t^2 e^{-t}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d \\mathrm{I}}{d t}=2 t e^{-t}-e^{-t} t^2=e^{-t} t(2-t) \\\\\n& e=-\\mathrm{L} \\frac{d \\mathrm{I}}{d t} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{d \\mathrm{I}}{d t}=0 \\Rightarrow e^{-t} t(2-t)=0 \\\\\n& t=2 \\mathrm{sec}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
